                <pb facs="0594" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg490"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-02T11:00:00+08:00">March 2, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 2—3:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>294. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 1, 3 p.m. The establishment of the new state was announced
                            officially this morning by Chang Ching-hui at his residence at Mukden.
                            After painting a black picture of conditions in Manchuria and China
                            since the establishment of the Republic the proclamation announces the
                            complete severance of relations with the Republic of China and the
                            establishment of the state of Manchoukuo as well as the fundamental
                            principles on which the new state is established including
                            acknowledgment of debt obligations of the territory and the principles
                            of the open door and equal opportunity.</p>
                        <p>It was announced that foreign governments will be notified
                            officially.</p>
                        <p>The Japanese press today state that the inauguration of Pu will occur on
                            March 10th. Myers.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
